ESP: non-DMA data transfers

A transfer-information command in the data-out phase without DMA wasn't
implemented and aborted the emulator: send the FIFO contents to the
target and interrupt for more.  In the data-in phase, the interrupt
didn't report bus service.  Linux's ESP driver uses programmed I/O for
transfers that aren't whole 16-byte DMA bursts.

Upstream candidate.

--- src/esp.c
+++ src/esp.c
@@ -863,8 +863,17 @@
         switch (SCSIbus.phase) {
             case PHASE_DI:
                 esp_fifo_write(SCSIdisk_Send_Data());
+                intstatus = INTR_BS;
                 CycInt_AddCyclesEvent(20, EVENT_ESP_INTERRUPT);
                 break;
+            case PHASE_DO:
+                /* Send the FIFO contents, then interrupt for more */
+                while (fifoflags > 0 && SCSIbus.phase == PHASE_DO) {
+                    SCSIdisk_Receive_Data(esp_fifo_read());
+                }
+                intstatus = INTR_BS;
+                CycInt_AddCyclesEvent(20, EVENT_ESP_INTERRUPT);
+                break;
             case PHASE_MI:
                 CycInt_AddCyclesEvent(20, EVENT_ESP_INTERRUPT);
                 break;
